Z||000011||olympic||06-02-2000||09:57 PM||||hmmmm, lets see here 3.0l V12=15 cubic inches/cylinder.  Bore and stroke would be about 2.7"(assuming they were equal).  And they fit 4 or 5 valves in that 2.7" bore yet, it's insane what these guys can build.<BR>   770hp@18000 rpm means it has 225 lb-feet of torque at 18000 rpm also.  Seems strange to see numbers like that because street engines usually produce more torque than HP.<BR>   As for the sound, yeah, what Monkeyman said!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
